# Build context for the container image.
#
# The image builds the storefront from `web/` (the Dockerfile's first stage),
# so the app sources and the lockfile must be IN here — they used to be
# excluded, back when the image expected a pre-built `web/out` copied in from
# the build machine. What stays out is what the container never runs:
# host-built `node_modules`, the dev server's `.next`, the live data dir, the
# retired paths under `archive/`, and the decision/capture/docs material that
# is not code.
#
# A pattern with no slash matches at ANY depth here, exactly as Docker does it.
# So a line reading `games` would also remove `web/public/games` — every cover
# the lobby cards load — and the build would still succeed. Do not add a bare
# name that is also a runtime directory; `python scripts/docker_context.py`
# fails the build early if one ever slips in.

.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
archive
decisions
docs
scripts

# the provider catalogue ships; its fetch caches are machine state
probes/*cache*.json

# build output and dev-server caches: the image builds its own copy
web/node_modules
web/.next
web/out
web/README.md

# the live ledger, profiles, rounds and admin sessions
demo/data

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
*.md